# Operations

## Health

- Liveness and readiness path: `/actuator/health`
- Metrics path: `/actuator/metrics`
- Application port: `8080`

## High Availability

The generated Helm chart defaults to two replicas, rolling updates, resource requests, probes, and a PodDisruptionBudget. Keep `replicaCount` at `2` or higher for production.

## Security

- Never commit `.env`; use `.env.example` only for local setup.
- Store credentials outside the image.
- Run the container as the non-root app user provided by the Dockerfile.
- Review the generated transform artifact for accidental sensitive field propagation.

## Performance

- Keep transform artifacts under the 128 KB guardrail used by the local worker.
- Keep preview samples small and representative.
- Use bounded aggregation windows and explicit keys when building aggregation transforms.

## Build

```bash
mvn test
docker build -t {{ artifact_id }}:{{ service_version }} .
```

## Deploy

```bash
helm upgrade --install {{ service_name }} ./helm \
  --set image.repository={{ artifact_id }} \
  --set image.tag={{ service_version }}
```
